### 3. Reviewing the Data Synchronization Pipeline
With these enhancements in place, creating a batch via the frontend will log "Created" under LAST_ACTION.
When a PENDING_L1 checker approves it, the application evaluates the current step's metadata, detects "Verifier", and generates "Approved by Verifier" inside the transaction journal.
The state data now flows from the database through the execution context directly into your frontend layouts without hardcoded definitions.
